From edca07ab88b27f18c0ad94683b2f51e548df6fd9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 08:57:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Let an admin change what one person can do
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Team members already had a role, but a role was all or nothing: the one
senior agent trusted with imports had to be made an admin, which handed
them everything else too.

Each person's profile now has a "What they can do" card listing four
things — import listings, publish listings, delete listings, export
data. They start from whatever the role normally allows and an admin
can change any of them for that person alone. Only the differences are
stored, so anyone left on their role's defaults keeps following those
defaults.

The buttons and menu entries follow the same rule, so someone who
cannot import no longer sees an Import link that would only refuse
them. Every permission is enforced on the route as well, not only
hidden in the page.

An admin's own boxes are fixed on and the form refuses to save against
an admin account. An admin who removed their own access to the team
screen could not get it back without a database editor.

Note this changes a default: importing was open to anyone signed in and
is now admin-only, grantable per person.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
